.TH STREAMLINE-FIND 1 "Jan 2026" "streamline-vectors" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
streamline-find \- search Streamline icon collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B streamline-find
.I QUERY...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B streamline-find
searches through the Streamline icon collection and returns matching SVG
pathnames with match rankings. Results are ordered by relevance score in
descending order.
.PP
The tool uses a SQLite search index when available for fast searching. If no
index is found, it falls back to filesystem search (consider running
.BR streamline-index (1)
to build the search index for better performance).
.PP
The search supports multiple query types:
.TP
.B Filename search
Exact filename matches, prefix matches, and partial matches
.TP
.B Category search
Search by main categories (plump, core, flex, sharp, ultimate, block, etc.)
.TP
.B Style search
Search by visual styles (duo, flat, gradient, solid, etc.) for styled categories
.TP
.B Subcategory search
Search by functional subcategories (culture, arrows, interface-essential, etc.)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -r, --rank
Print rank score along with each result.
.TP
.B -f, --full-path
Print full absolute path instead of relative path from data directory.
.TP
.B -o, --or
Use OR logic instead of AND for multiple query terms.
.TP
.B -i, --index =\fIFILE\fR
Specify the index file to use (default: /var/lib/streamline-vectors/index.db).
.TP
.B -d, --data-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Specify the icon data directory to use (default: /usr/share/streamline-vectors).
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Decrease verbosity. Can be used multiple times.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Increase verbosity. Can be used multiple times.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show version information and exit.
.PP
All other arguments are treated as search query terms. By default, multiple
terms use AND logic (all terms must match). Use \fB-o\fR/\fB--or\fR for OR logic
(any term must match).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STREAMLINE_INDEX
Path to the search index database (default: /var/lib/streamline-vectors/index.db)
.TP
.B STREAMLINE_DATA_DIR
Path to the icon data directory (default: /usr/share/streamline-vectors)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Search for arrows:
.B streamline-find arrow
.TP
Search by category:
.B streamline-find plump
.TP
Search by style:
.B streamline-find duo
.TP
Search by subcategory:
.B streamline-find culture
.TP
Search for specific icon:
.B streamline-find coffee
.TP
Search for icons matching both "coffee" AND "bold" (default AND logic):
.B streamline-find coffee bold
.TP
Search for icons matching either "coffee" OR "bold" (OR logic):
.B streamline-find -o coffee bold
.TP
Show ranking scores:
.B streamline-find -r coffee
.TP
Show full absolute paths:
.B streamline-find -f coffee
.TP
Use custom index file:
.B streamline-find -i /path/to/custom/index.db coffee
.TP
Use custom data directory:
.B streamline-find -d /path/to/icons coffee
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/streamline-vectors/index.db
SQLite search index (built by streamline-index)
.TP
.I /usr/share/streamline-vectors/
Icon data directory
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR streamline-index (1)
